---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import galleryCategory from "../../assets/rocky-concrete/gallery-category.png";
import gallerySubcategories from "../../assets/rocky-concrete/gallery-subcategories.png";
import galleryLanding from "../../assets/rocky-concrete/gallery-landing.png";

const photoSteps = [
  {
    label: "His iPhone",
    sub: "HEIC photos, on-site",
    color: "gray",
    icon: "phone",
  },
  {
    label: "Custom Upload",
    sub: "Simple form, HEIC→JPEG in-browser, Spanish-friendly",
    color: "violet",
    icon: "upload",
  },
  {
    label: "Sanity CMS",
    sub: "Embedded studio, schemas, references",
    color: "violet",
    icon: "cms",
  },
  {
    label: "SSR + CDN Cache",
    sub: "Stale-while-revalidate, served instantly from the edge",
    color: "violet",
    icon: "bolt",
  },
  {
    label: "Visitor's Browser",
    sub: "Instant load from warm cache",
    color: "gray",
    icon: "globe",
  },
];

import Section from "./Section.astro";
import Prose from "./Prose.astro";
import Column from "./Column.astro";
import Wide from "./Wide.astro";
---

<!-- The System: pipeline diagram + performance -->
<Section title="The System">
  <Prose class="mb-8">
    <p>
      The gallery is the whole pitch. A contractor charging five figures for a
      patio can't have a site that loads like it was cheap to make, so fast
      wasn't a nice-to-have, it was the product. The catch is that a gallery is
      the heaviest kind of page there is: dozens of high-res photos plus video,
      the slowest stuff to load.
    </p>
    <p>
      It also has the most moving parts, so I built it as a pipeline and
      designed each layer around who's using it: he posts from the admin side,
      his customers browse from the public side, and a cache in the middle keeps
      every visitor's load fast.
    </p>
  </Prose>

  <!-- Diagram container -->
  <Wide
    class="bg-gradient-to-br from-gray-50 to-violet-50/40 rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-10 border border-gray-200"
  >
    <!-- Main flow: photos -->
    <div class="mb-8">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-4">
        <span
          class="px-2.5 py-1 bg-violet-100 text-violet-700 text-xs font-semibold rounded-full border border-violet-200"
        >
          PHOTO PATH
        </span>
      </div>

      <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row items-stretch gap-3">
        {
          photoSteps.map((step, i) => (
            <>
              <div
                class:list={[
                  "flex-1 bg-white rounded-2xl p-4 border shadow-sm",
                  step.color === "violet" && "border-violet-200",
                  step.color === "amber" && "border-amber-300",
                  step.color === "gray" && "border-gray-200",
                ]}
              >
                <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-1.5">
                  <div
                    class:list={[
                      "w-7 h-7 rounded-lg flex items-center justify-center shrink-0",
                      step.color === "violet" && "bg-violet-100",
                      step.color === "amber" && "bg-amber-100",
                      step.color === "gray" && "bg-gray-100",
                    ]}
                  >
                    {step.icon === "phone" && (
                      <svg
                        class:list={[
                          "w-4 h-4",
                          step.color === "violet" && "text-violet-600",
                          step.color === "amber" && "text-amber-700",
                          step.color === "gray" && "text-gray-600",
                        ]}
                        fill="none"
                        stroke="currentColor"
                        viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                      >
                        <path
                          stroke-linecap="round"
                          stroke-linejoin="round"
                          stroke-width="2"
                          d="M12 18h.01M8 21h8a2 2 0 002-2V5a2 2 0 00-2-2H8a2 2 0 00-2 2v14a2 2 0 002 2z"
                        />
                      </svg>
                    )}
                    {step.icon === "upload" && (
                      <svg
                        class:list={[
                          "w-4 h-4",
                          step.color === "violet" && "text-violet-600",
                        ]}
                        fill="none"
                        stroke="currentColor"
                        viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                      >
                        <path
                          stroke-linecap="round"
                          stroke-linejoin="round"
                          stroke-width="2"
                          d="M4 16v1a3 3 0 003 3h10a3 3 0 003-3v-1m-4-8l-4-4m0 0L8 8m4-4v12"
                        />
                      </svg>
                    )}
                    {step.icon === "cms" && (
                      <svg
                        class:list={[
                          "w-4 h-4",
                          step.color === "violet" && "text-violet-600",
                        ]}
                        fill="none"
                        stroke="currentColor"
                        viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                      >
                        <path
                          stroke-linecap="round"
                          stroke-linejoin="round"
                          stroke-width="2"
                          d="M4 7v10c0 2 1 3 3 3h10c2 0 3-1 3-3V7c0-2-1-3-3-3H7c-2 0-3 1-3 3zm0 4h16M9 4v16"
                        />
                      </svg>
                    )}
                    {step.icon === "bolt" && (
                      <svg
                        class="w-4 h-4 text-violet-600"
                        fill="none"
                        stroke="currentColor"
                        viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                      >
                        <path
                          stroke-linecap="round"
                          stroke-linejoin="round"
                          stroke-width="2"
                          d="M13 10V3L4 14h7v7l9-11h-7z"
                        />
                      </svg>
                    )}
                    {step.icon === "globe" && (
                      <svg
                        class="w-4 h-4 text-gray-600"
                        fill="none"
                        stroke="currentColor"
                        viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                      >
                        <path
                          stroke-linecap="round"
                          stroke-linejoin="round"
                          stroke-width="2"
                          d="M3.055 11H5a2 2 0 012 2v1a2 2 0 002 2 2 2 0 012 2v2.945M8 3.935V5.5A2.5 2.5 0 0010.5 8h.5a2 2 0 012 2 2 2 0 104 0 2 2 0 012-2h1.064M15 20.488V18a2 2 0 012-2h3.064M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"
                        />
                      </svg>
                    )}
                  </div>
                  <div class="text-gray-900 font-semibold text-sm">
                    {step.label}
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="text-gray-500 text-xs leading-snug">{step.sub}</div>
              </div>
              {i < photoSteps.length - 1 && (
                <div class="flex items-center justify-center md:px-0 px-0">
                  <svg
                    class="w-5 h-5 text-gray-400 rotate-90 md:rotate-0"
                    fill="none"
                    stroke="currentColor"
                    viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                  >
                    <path
                      stroke-linecap="round"
                      stroke-linejoin="round"
                      stroke-width="2.5"
                      d="M9 5l7 7-7 7"
                    />
                  </svg>
                </div>
              )}
            </>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </Wide>

  <Prose class="mt-8">
    <p>
      <strong class="font-semibold text-gray-900"
        >No rebuild when he posts.</strong
      >
      Moving to Sanity took his content off the repo, which was half the rebuild
      problem. The pages were the other half: while the site was statically generated,
      every photo he posted meant a production deploy on Netlify, a flat 15 credits
      each against a 300-credit monthly cap that pauses the site when it runs out.
      That's about 20 photos a month before the gallery goes dark, on a site he updates
      after almost every job. So I dropped the static build, replaced <code
        class="font-mono text-[0.92em] text-violet-700 bg-violet-50 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded"
        >getStaticPaths</code
      > with validation at request time, and moved the pages to server rendering.
      Now an upload writes straight to the CMS and never triggers a deploy.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong class="font-semibold text-gray-900"
        >On top of that, a cache keeps server rendering fast.</strong
      > The pages sit behind a stale-while-revalidate cache (<code
        class="font-mono text-[0.92em] text-violet-700 bg-violet-50 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded"
        >s-maxage=1, stale-while-revalidate=30d</code
      >), so visitors load instantly from the CDN while new content re-renders
      in the background and appears a request later.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong class="font-semibold text-gray-900"
        >The video player never blocks the first load.</strong
      > Each video sits in the grid as a static thumbnail. The actual Mux player
      is dynamically imported and built only when someone opens the lightbox, so
      it's never in the initial bundle slowing down render. The hover preview works
      the same way: it only starts fetching when the thumbnail is about to enter
      the viewport, not on page load. Before I did this the page crawled on arrival
      because everything tried to load at once. Now the heavy stuff loads when it's
      actually needed.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong class="font-semibold text-gray-900"
        >Everything else is keeping bytes off the page until they're needed.</strong
      > Photos come off his phone at full size (~2–5MB each). I serve them through
      Sanity's image CDN resized to the size they actually display, with <code
        class="font-mono text-[0.92em] text-violet-700 bg-violet-50 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded"
        >auto('format')</code
      > handing browsers WebP or AVIF, so a multi-megabyte photo lands around 50KB.
      The first row loads eagerly so something's on screen right away, everything
      below it is lazy-loaded, and the rest sits behind a "load more" so a visitor
      isn't downloading a hundred photos to see the first twelve.
    </p>
  </Prose>

  <!-- Lighthouse scorecard -->
  <Column class="mt-8">
    <p
      class="text-xs font-semibold text-gray-400 uppercase tracking-widest mb-3"
    >
      Lighthouse
    </p>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-3">
      <div
        class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white px-4 py-4 text-center shadow-sm"
      >
        <div class="text-3xl font-bold text-emerald-600">99</div>
        <div class="mt-1 text-xs text-gray-500">Performance</div>
      </div>
      <div
        class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white px-4 py-4 text-center shadow-sm"
      >
        <div class="text-3xl font-bold text-emerald-600">98</div>
        <div class="mt-1 text-xs text-gray-500">Accessibility</div>
      </div>
      <div
        class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white px-4 py-4 text-center shadow-sm"
      >
        <div class="text-3xl font-bold text-emerald-600">100</div>
        <div class="mt-1 text-xs text-gray-500">Best Practices</div>
      </div>
      <div
        class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white px-4 py-4 text-center shadow-sm"
      >
        <div class="text-3xl font-bold text-emerald-600">100</div>
        <div class="mt-1 text-xs text-gray-500">SEO</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-8 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed text-lg">
      The payoff: A site that feels as premium as the work in it.
    </p>
  </Column>

  <!-- What the visitor lands on -->
  <Wide class="mt-8 grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-6 items-start">
    <figure class="sm:col-start-1 sm:row-start-1">
      <Image
        src={galleryLanding}
        alt="The gallery landing on rockyconcreteinc.com: a Browse by Category grid of six service categories, each with a cover photo, above a curated Featured strip."
        class="w-full rounded-xl border border-gray-200 shadow-sm"
      />
      <figcaption class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-500 leading-relaxed">
        The landing page for gallery: six categories, each with a cover I set in
        the Studio, over a curated Featured strip.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure class="sm:col-start-1 sm:row-start-2">
      <Image
        src={galleryCategory}
        alt="The Concrete Work category page on rockyconcreteinc.com: a top nav of service categories, with the Walkways & Steps photos showing 6 of 8 before a load-more."
        class="w-full rounded-xl border border-gray-200 shadow-sm"
      />
      <figcaption class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-500 leading-relaxed">
        A category page: his services across the top, the work below.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure class="sm:col-start-2 sm:row-start-1 sm:row-span-2">
      <Image
        src={gallerySubcategories}
        alt="A category broken into subcategories (Walkways & Steps, Flatwork & Patios, Stone Work), each its own grid of finished jobs with a load-more."
        class="w-full rounded-xl border border-gray-200 shadow-sm"
      />
      <figcaption class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-500 leading-relaxed">
        Each category breaks into subcategories, each loading a batch at a time.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </Wide>
</Section>
